# Sheet layout lock

The morning sheet stays on one A4. Do not change the layout, the grid, or these counts unless Alessandro explicitly asks to change the layout.

## Grid

Top band: weather in the narrow left track, agenda wider beside it, news the widest track down the full right side.
Middle band, above the mail: health and reminders side by side, each about half of the width under weather plus agenda.
Bottom band: email spans the full page width, including the space under the news column. The bands above size to their text; leftover height belongs to the mail. Subject and body may use two lines. Three mail columns on the wide sheet. Agenda day cards are one column, on screen and in the PDF.

## Counts

- Agenda: 4 day cards.
- News: 7. Up to three lines under each title.
- Reminders: 3.
- Email: 2 rows × 3 columns, 6 cards. No third mail row. No sentence under the cards. Notable cards only fill empty cells inside those six.
- Health column: sleep, arterial pressure, and activity, each with a judgment and one piece of advice. A general line only when something else is off or getting worse. No figures, no device names, no "not from yesterday" preface.

Screen, PDF capture, and print use the same map.
